div class="font-mono whitespace-pre leading-6"><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus" style="background-color:#ffffff;--shiki-dark-bg:#0B0C0E;color:#1f2328;--shiki-dark:#D4D4D4" language="text"><code language="text" numberOfLines="2"><span class="line"><span>Available commands: [&quot;clear&quot;, &quot;compact&quot;, &quot;context&quot;, &quot;usage&quot;, &quot;code-review&quot;, &quot;verify&quot;, &quot;security-check&quot;, ...]</span></span>
<span class="line"><span></span></span></code></pre></div></div></div></div><div class="code-block-fade-overlay print:hidden" data-fade-overlay="true" aria-hidden="true" style="--fade-color-light:#ffffff;--fade-color-dark:#0B0C0E"></div></div>
<span data-as="p">A skill with <a class="link" href="/docs/en/skills#control-who-invokes-a-skill"><code>user-invocable: false</code></a> in its frontmatter doesn’t appear in this list or in the <code>skills</code> array from <a href="#confirm-skills-loaded" class="link">Confirm skills loaded</a>. Sessions that configure <a class="link" href="/docs/en/agent-sdk/mcp">MCP servers</a> can also expose <a class="link" href="/docs/en/mcp#use-mcp-prompts-as-commands">MCP prompts as commands</a>.</span>
<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="dispatch-commands-by-name"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#dispatch-commands-by-name" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="2" class="size-3 shrink-0"><use href="#mi-mint-1-Link"></use></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">Dispatch commands by name</span></h3>
<span data-as="p">Send a command by including it in your prompt string, the same way you send regular text. Dispatch doesn’t depend on the <code>skills</code> option. Sending <code>/&lt;name&gt;</code> runs a user-invocable skill even when your <code>skills</code> list omits it. Commands that act on conversation history, such as <code>/compact</code>, need prior messages to work with.</span>
<span data-as="p">A <code>/&lt;name&gt;</code> that matches neither a command in the session nor a built-in Claude Code command doesn’t fail the query. Claude Code sends the prompt to Claude as an ordinary message, with a note that the command didn’t run, so the query spends a model turn and returns Claude’s reply. Before v2.1.274, a <code>/&lt;name&gt;</code> that matched nothing returned <code>Unknown command: /&lt;name&gt;</code> as the result without a model turn.</span>
<span data-as="p">A <code>/&lt;name&gt;</code> that matches a built-in Claude Code command that isn’t available in the session, such as <code>/theme</code>, returns <code>/theme isn&#x27;t available in this environment.</code> as the result without a model turn.</span>
<div role="note" aria-label="Note" class="callout my-4 px-5 py-4 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl flex gap-3 border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50 dark:border-blue-900 dark:bg-blue-600/20" data-callout-type="note"><div class="mt-0.5 w-4" data-component-part="callout-icon"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="1.5" class="size-4 text-blue-800 dark:text-blue-300"><use href="#mi-mint-1-CalloutNote"></use></svg></div><div class="text-sm prose dark:prose-invert min-w-0 w-full [&amp;_kbd]:bg-background-light dark:[&amp;_kbd]:bg-background-dark [&amp;_code]:text-current! [&amp;_kbd]:text-current! [&amp;_a]:text-current! [&amp;_a]:border-current [&amp;_strong]:text-current! text-blue-800 dark:text-blue-300" data-component-part="callout-content"><span data-as="p">A command can hit the <code>maxTurns</code> / <code>max_turns</code> limit like any other prompt, ending the query with an error result instead of <code>success</code>. For the error-result contract, see <a class="link" href="/docs/en/agent-sdk/agent-loop#handle-the-result">Handle the result</a>. If your command might hit the limit, wrap the loop in a <code>try</code>/<code>catch</code> in TypeScript or <code>try</code>/<code>except</code> in Python, as shown in <a class="link" href="/docs/en/agent-sdk/streaming-vs-single-mode#single-message-input">Single Message Input</a>, or set <code>maxTurns</code> high enough for the work to complete.</span></div></div>
<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="compact-history-with-/compact"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#compact-history-with-/compact" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="2" class="size-3 shrink-0"><use href="#mi-mint-1-Link"></use></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">Compact history with <code>/compact</code></span></h3>
<span data-as="p">The <code>/compact</code> command reduces the size of your conversation history by summarizing older messages while preserving important context. Compaction needs an existing conversation with enough prior messages to summarize. This example has a conversation first, then compacts it and reads the <code>compact_boundary</code> system message that reports the result:</span>
<div data-orientation="horizontal" data-activation-direction="none" class="code-group p-0.5 mt-5 mb-8 flex flex-col not-prose relative rounded-2xl border border-gray-950/10 dark:border-white/10 min-w-0 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-white/5 dark:codeblock-dark text-gray-950 dark:text-gray-50 codeblock-light"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 relative pr-2.5" data-component-part="code-group-tab-bar"><div role="presentation" style="position:relative;--scroll-area-corner-height:0px;--scroll-area-corner-width:0px" data-component-part="scroll-area" class="min-w-0 flex-1 w-0 rounded-tl-xl"><div data-id="base-ui-_R_alaaqqelubqoqe9qj4npfiutb_-viewport" tabindex="-1" class="size-full rounded-[inherit] [--scroll-area-fade-size:32px] overflow-y-hidden! base-ui-disable-scrollbar" style="overflow:scroll" data-component-part="scroll-area-viewport"><div role="presentation" style="min-width:fit-content" data-component-part="scroll-area-content"><div data-orientation="horizontal" data-activation-direction="none" role="tablist" aria-label="Code examples" class="text-xs leading-6 gap-1 flex"><button type="button" data-active="" data-orientation="horizontal" data-activation-direction="none" aria-disabled="false" tabindex="-1" role="tab" aria-selected="true" id="base-ui-_R_1dalaaqqelubqoqe9qj4npfiutb_" data-composite-item-active="" class="group flex items-center relative gap-1.5 my-1 mb-1.5 outline-0 whitespace-nowrap font-medium ml-0! first:ml-2.5! focus-visible:outline-hidden text-primary dark:text-primary-light"><div class="peer/title flex items-center gap-1.5 px-1.5 rounded-lg z-10 group-focus-visible:outline-1 group-focus-visible:outline-primary dark:group-focus-visible:outline-primary-light group-hover:bg-gray-200/50 dark:group-hover:bg-gray-700/70 group-hover:text-primary dark:group-hover:text-primary-light">TypeScript</div><div class="absolute -bottom-1.5 left-0 right-0 h-0.5 rounded-full bg-primary dark:bg-primary-light peer-empty/title:hidden"></div></button><button type="button" data-orientation="horizontal" data-activation-direction="none" aria-disabled="false" tabindex="-1" role="tab" aria-selected="false" id="base-ui-_R_2dalaaqqelubqoqe9qj4npfiutb_" class="group flex items-center relative gap-1.5 my-1 mb-1.5 outline-0 whitespace-nowrap font-medium ml-0! first:ml-2.5! focus-visible:outline-hidden text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400"><div class="peer/title flex items-center gap-1.5 px-1.5 rounded-lg z-10 group-focus-visible:outline-1 group-focus-visible:outline-primary dark:group-focus-visible:outline-primary-light group-hover:bg-gray-200/50 dark:group-hover:bg-gray-700/70 group-hover:text-primary dark:group-hover:text-primary-light">Python</div></button></div></div></div></div><div class="flex items-center justify-end shrink-0 gap-1.5"><div class="z-10 select-none" id="base-ui-_R_3qilaaqqelubqoqe9qj4npfiutb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><button class="size-6.5 flex items-center justify-center rounded-md group/code-snippet-feedback-button [.code-block_[data-floating-buttons]_&amp;]:bg-gray-100 dark:[.code-block_[data-floating-buttons]_&amp;]:bg-gray-800 [.code-block:has([data-fade-overlay])_[data-floating-buttons]_&amp;]:bg-transparent dark:[.code-block:has([data-fade-overlay])_[data-floating-buttons]_&amp;]:bg-transparent" id="code-snippet-feedback-button" aria-label="Report incorrect code"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="1.5" class="size-4 shrink-0 text-gray-400 group-hover/code-snippet-feedback-button:text-gray-500 dark:text-white/40 dark:group-hover/code-snippet-feedback-button:text-white/60"><use href="#mi-mint-1-Report"></use></svg></button></div><div class="code-block-copy-button z-10 select-none" id="base-ui-_R_3rilaaqqelubqoqe9qj4npfiutb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><button class="size-6.5 flex items-center justify-center rounded-md group/copy-button [.code-block_[data-floating-buttons]_&amp;]:bg-gray-100 dark:[.code-block_[data-floating-buttons]_&amp;]:bg-gray-800 [.code-block:has([dat