,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`allow-only-specific-skills`,children:`Allow only specific skills`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`To let Claude invoke only specific skills, pass their names in the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`skills`}),` list:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Your own skills`}),`: the skill’s directory name`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Plugin skills`}),`: `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`plugin:skill`})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsxs(_components.strong,{children:[`Name clashes in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`additionalDirectories`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`add_dirs`})]}),`: a skill in one of those directories gets a `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/skills#how-a-skill-gets-its-command-name`,children:`prefixed name`}),` when its name clashes with an enterprise, personal, or project skill, or one in a directory added earlier. List it by that name. With a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`verify`}),` skill in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`../api`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`../web`}),`, added in that order, and no other `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`verify`}),` skill, list them as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`verify`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`web:verify`}),`. Requires Claude Code v2.1.309 or later`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The list takes exact skill names only. If an entry can’t work as an exact name, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`query()`}),` rejects the list before the session starts. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#invalid-skill-name-error`,children:`Invalid skill name error`}),` for the name rules and the error each SDK raises.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The model doesn’t see unlisted skills and the Skill tool rejects them, while their files remain on disk and stay reachable through Read and Bash. Restricting the list doesn’t restrict `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#dispatch-commands-by-name`,children:`dispatch by name`}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`To let Claude invoke every discovered skill, pass `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`skills: \"all\"`}),` rather than a wildcard.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`commands-in-agent-sdk-sessions`,children:`Commands in Agent SDK sessions`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`This section is the SDK’s command documentation. A command is anything you run by sending `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/\u003cname\u003e`}),` in a prompt. Entries on the command surface differ in what backs them:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Built-in commands`}),`: execute logic coded into the Claude Code process the SDK runs, for example `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/compact`})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Bundled skills`}),`: prompt artifacts included with Claude Code, for example `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/code-review`})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Your skills`}),`: prompt artifacts that you author, each a directory holding a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`SKILL.md`}),` file. A user-invocable skill’s name joins the surface automatically, so dispatching your own `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/security-check`}),` and running a built-in work the same way`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Custom command files`}),`: an older artifact form with the same behavior, flat Markdown files in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`.claude/commands/`}),` whose filenames become command names. Skills are their recommended successor`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`By default, both you and Claude can invoke any skill. You can restrict either path through the skill’s `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/skills#control-who-invokes-a-skill`,children:`frontmatter`}),`. For definitions of command and skill, see the glossary’s `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/glossary#command`,children:`Command`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/glossary#skill`,children:`Skill`}),` entries. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/commands`,children:`Commands in Claude Code`}),` for every built-in and `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/skills`,children:`Extend Claude with skills`}),` for the complete guide to both artifact forms.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`discover-available-commands`,children:`Discover available commands`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`You can dispatch commands that work without an interactive terminal through the SDK. The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`system/init`}),` message lists the ones available in your session in its `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`slash_commands`}),` field. Commands that need an interactive terminal, such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/theme`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/terminal-setup`}),`, don’t appear in the list. Access the field when your session starts:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(CodeGroup,{children:[_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:`TypeScript`,numberOfLines:`10`,language:`typescript`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`typescript`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`typescript`,numberOfLines:`10`,children:[_jsxs(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#CF222E`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#C586C0`},children:`import`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:` { `}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#9CDCFE`},children:`query`}),_jsx(_components.span,{style:{color:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},childre