hen the session holds a prompt but no reply from Claude yet. A fresh one-shot `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`query()`}),` call starts with empty context, so use this pattern in a session with prior turns, for example in `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/agent-sdk/streaming-vs-single-mode`,children:`streaming input mode`}),` or when resuming a session.`]})}),`\n`,_jsxs(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`reset-context-with-/clear`,children:[`Reset context with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/clear`})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/clear`}),` command resets the conversation to an empty context, so subsequent prompts start with no prior conversation history. The previous conversation remains on disk. You can return to that conversation by passing its session ID to the `,_jsxs(_components.a,{href:`/en/agent-sdk/sessions#resume-by-id`,children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`resume`}),` option`]}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/clear`}),` is useful in `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/en/agent-sdk/streaming-vs-single-mode`,children:`streaming input mode`}),`, where you send multiple prompts over a single connection. For one-shot `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`query()`}),` calls, each call already starts with empty context, so sending `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/clear`}),` has no practical effect. Start a new `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`query()`}),` instead.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`create-skills`,children:`Create skills`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Create each skill as a directory containing a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`SKILL.md`}),` file with YAML frontmatter and Markdown content. The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`description`}),` field determines when Claude invokes your skill.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Example directory structure`}),`:`]}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLi